# `GENRE-CONNECTOR-SPELLING`: `edge` under `flowchart` is a LINE ERROR with a NAMED diagnostic —
# not `unrecognized line`, and not the bare allowlist message. The author has
# written a real construct under the wrong spelling, so the message names the
# word this genre uses and why, which the generic "not allowed in genre" does
# not. `state` is rejected here too: flowchart keeps `node`.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
process a "Step"
process b "Step 2"
edge a -> b
state c "C"
